+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<token>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`: items ordered by `id`, with a
+  default limit of 20. Follow `next_cursor` as the next request's `cursor`;
+  it is `null` on the last page. Omit `cursor` on the first request. Invalid
+  limits or cursors return status 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
